# Packages that must never be installed in the image (pinned to -1 during the
# build, purged if a dependency pulled them in). The pin is removed before
# the image is packed, so users can still install them later.
#
# Only list packages nothing in the image *depends* on — purging a
# dependency removes the packages that need it (e.g. Lutris depends on
# fluid-soundfont-gs, so the soundfont cannot be excluded).

# Duplicate Wine: Lutris only *recommends* it; the image ships stable 'wine'
wine-development
libwine-development

# GNOME's session stack, pulled in as recommendations and first alternatives
# (network-manager-gnome: "gnome-shell | polkit agent", blueman:
# "notification-daemon"). PRIMERS OS is an Openbox desktop: these add
# hundreds of MB, and their login-screen sessions would let a candidate
# pick a desktop instead of the Exam Mode kiosk. Real alternatives are in
# base.list (lxpolkit, notification-daemon).
gdm3
ubuntu-session
gnome-shell
gnome-session-bin
gnome-control-center
gnome-settings-daemon
